===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[united|United]] [[nation|Nations]]|def=1}}

# {{lb|en|singular}} An [[international]] [[coalition]], founded in 1945 and headquartered in [[New York City]], that aims to promote global co-operation and maintain international order.
#* {{quote-av
|en
|date=September 1, 1950
|author=w:Harry S. Truman
|title=MP72-73 Korea and World Peace: President Truman Reports to the People
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fMDAbVD9yx0
|publisher=w:Harry S. Truman Presidential Library and Museum
|id=National Archives Identifier: [https://catalog.archives.gov/id/595162 595162]
|time=3:28
|text=We hope in particular that the people of China will not be misled or forced into fighting against the '''United Nations''' and against the American people, who have always been and still are their friends.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2007
|author=w:Joe Biden
|title={{w|Promises to Keep (Biden book)|Promises to Keep}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/promisestokeepon00joeb/
|year_published=2008
|location=[[New York]]
|publisher=w:Random House
|ISBN=978-0-8129-7621-2
|LCCN=2007019603
|OCLC=1262796254
|page=117
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/promisestokeepon00joeb/page/117/
|text={{smallcaps|jill and i were married by a catholic priest at the}} '''United Nations''' chapel in New York City in June 1977.}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|plural|historical}} The [[Allies]] of [[World War II]]; the [[country|countries]] [[fight]]ing against the [[Axis Powers]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=23 February 1942|title=Dutchman's Chance|url=http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,884450,00.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20080307112423/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,884450,00.html|archivedate=7 March 2008|accessdate=13 December 2022|work={{w|Time (magazine)|TIME}}|text=Last week plump Admiral Helfrich was not at sea, but in the '''United Nations'''{{'}} well-guarded, teeming headquarters in interior Java. Under him, in the top sea command, was a U.S. naval officer whom Admiral Helfrich and all the Dutch had learned to admire: 55-year-old Vice Admiral William A. Glassford Jr. Admiral Glassford needed more cruisers, more destroyers, more submarines for the sea defense of Java. Admiral Helfrich needed men & munitions, but especially aircraft and airmen.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Information Service|url=https://archive.org/details/sim_information-services_1943-11-27_22_39/mode/1up|volume=XXII|issue=39|location=New York, N.Y.|date=27 November 1943|passage='''United Nations''' Plan Their Domestic Economies / All the '''United Nations''' are determined that out of this war shall come a finer and richer life for the average citizen, according to a survey of ''Postwar Plans of the United Nations'' by Lewis L. Lorwin which The Twentieth Century Fund (New York) issued this week.}}
#* {{quote-song|1=en|year=1944|lyricist=Harold Jacob Rome|composer=Dmitri Dmitrievich Shostakovich|title=The '''United Nations'''|format=[[w:gramophone record|SP record]]|location=N.Y., U.S.A.|publisher=Keynote Recordings, Inc.|oclc=51334463|artist=Paul Robeson; Keynote Orchestra And Chorus|text='''United Nations''' on the march with flags unfurled<br>Together fight for victory, a free new world|note=M 1200 B}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:John Gilbert Winant|[John Gilbert] Winant]]|chapter=The Ambassador in the United Kingdom (Winant) to the Secretary of State|title=Foreign Relations of the United States: Diplomatic Papers, 1945|volume=!III (European Advisory Commission; Austria; Germany)|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|United States Government Printing Office]]|date=20 April 1945|year_published=1968|page=234|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dw-YOTaoqWoC&pg=PA234|passage=Norway feels that imposition of terms “in the interests” of the '''United Nations''' other than the principal three powers leaves doubt regarding position of other '''United Nations''' towards Germany and may be source of juridical and political conflicts. [[w:Trygve Lie|[Trygve] Lie]] feels terms should state that in principle all '''United Nations''' are entitled to same rights towards Germany. Allies who have made valuable contribution to common victory should take part in notifying terms of surrender to the Germans.}}

